WEBVTT

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.700
What are you so depressed over, Nozomu?

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.210
Don’t ask me…

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:50.620
Don’t tell me you expected to make the top 30.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.570
That’s just hopeless.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:55.710
No, it’s not about my grades…{putting my grades aside…

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.100
Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan are pretty smart. So are Kira-chan and her sister.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.970
Well, their brains must be wired differently from ours.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.190
Gonda-san, congratulations!

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.960
Although you missed the top 30, this is still 100 times better than last time.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.350
That’s fabulous!

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.320
Hmm? Still!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.700
To enter the same school as the Ichijou sisters means that I have to study more.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.780
You guys study hard too.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.090
Yeah!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.270
The Ichijou Fan-Club’s… brave.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.590
Hmm? What’s the matter?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.090
At this rate, can I make it to the same high-school as everyone?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.540
Now then, everyone… this is your last summer as middle school students.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.110
Study and play, but keep your objectives in mind.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.180
And try not to do anything you’ll regret.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:49.650
Objectives, huh? I guess I’d better study more. Yet…

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.700
I know! Once it’s summer, the three of us should go to the beach!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.350
The beach?

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.780
Yes, and I bought a new swimsuit too.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.500
The three of us together, right?

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.450
Yes, the three of us together.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.250
I really want to go to to the beach with them.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.370
Huh?

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.530
I’ve already decided what I’ll be doing for summer vacation.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.640
When you think of summer, you think of love!

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.180
I’ve set my goals high – I’ll win both Sakurazuki sisters in one fell swoop!

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.830
You try hard too, Nozomu.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.550
You’re set on the
Ichijou sisters, right?

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.210
And what’re you going
to do about the test?

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.720
I’ll study at home. I’m not going to study any more than necessary.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.650
Speaking of which, your home is a sushi store, right?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.300
Oh yeah! Our goal is to make a worldwide chain.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.910
First, we plan to expand to Hawaii!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.160
In that case, you should study more English.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.130
Yeah, no kidding.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.000
Nozomu-kun!

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.500
Sakurazuki-san!

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.250
I’m impressed.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.800
To ride in the Sakurazukis’ car…

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.180
No problem, we’re heading in the same direction after all.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.680
A school application form?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.840
That’s right. We’ll be applying to a cram school.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.100
Father’s trial #3: during the summer, study at a cram school.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.100
We’ll have a lot of trials during the summer. It’ll be difficult.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.220
But there’ll be some enjoyable experiences as well, won’t there, Kira-chan?

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.650
Yes, Yura-chan.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.660
Really? Like what? Like what?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.700
That’s a secret for now.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.910
What are you planning to do this summer, Nozomu-kun?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.390
Well, that’s…

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.750
Of course we’re going to study at a cram school as well! Right, Nozomu?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.250
I’m envious of your groundless levity.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.310
Didn’t you say you wouldn’t study any harder than necessary?

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:51.050
It’s fine, right? Now we can see the Sakurazukis every day this summer.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.850
Oh, let’s go.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.780
Oh, it’s the Ichijous.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.750
Who’s the guy with them?
That’s not our school’s uniform.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.970
Oh, Nozomu-chan!

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.250
And the Sakurazukis!

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.460
Nozomu?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.730
Eh? Yuuya?

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.910
It’s sure been a long time.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.460
So you returned, huh?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.620
Is that Keisuke from grade school?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.470
Yeah.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.730
Is he a friend of yours?

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.510
Yeah, we used to play a lot in kindergarten.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.890
His name is Hiyama Yuuya.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:34.980
These are the Sakurazukis: Kira-chan and Yura-chan.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:38.900
Pleasure to meet you. Are you going to take classes here?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.820
Well, yeah. You too, Yuuya?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:46.810
Yeah, I was just about to apply when I ran into the Ichijous here.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.050
It’s been so long, it was a real surprise.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.830
Since our class reunion last year?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.460
We were in the same class in elementary school.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.200
Ah. Are you guys
in the same middle school?

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.430
Yes.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.210
Which high school
will you be applying to?

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.800
I… well, how do I say this? That’s…

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.420
I haven’t decided yet.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.050
Is that so?

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.440
Where are you aiming for, Yuuya-kun?

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.060
I’m trying for Hokunan University’s annex.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.830
You’re trying for something that difficult?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.040
Well, it’s part of the university –

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.440
they go by the Escalator System from entry to graduation.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:22.320
Escalator System: Allows students to bypass college entrance exams, but schools using it are usually more difficult.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.320
Even if it’s an annex, there are much easier places, aren’t there?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.950
The only place offering aeronautics is Hokunan University.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.120
Aeronautics?

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.070
That’s right. Rockets.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:39.760
When I grow up, I’m going to be the guy who makes rockets.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:40.910
What about you, Nozomu?

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:43.480
I’ll be someone who goes to the stars.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:47.730
Then I can take you to plenty of stars in my rocket!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:48.780
Okay.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:58.250
He really intended to be a rocket designer after all.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.270
I haven’t looked at the stars in a while…

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.780
Nozomu-kun! We have a watermelon, so come down and have some.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.460
Onii-chan, you’re slow!

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.740
Billy is going to eat all the tasty parts.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:18.250
I’m sorry. Huh?

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:20.420
Stop that, Billy!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.090
Hmmm? You’re taking extra classes?

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.250
Yeah…

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.890
Extra classes?

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.660
Onii-chan, you’re still studying even though it’s summer vacation?

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.480
That’s no fun.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.550
It’s finally summer…

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.150
Still, entry exam students
sure have it rough.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.370
You still have tests in cram school, right?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.110
And you’re divided into groups…

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.220
Huh? Is that right?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:56.600
It figures. I’ve let my grades slide so much,
I can’t be in the same class…

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.650
And on top of that…

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.730
Oh, we’re in the same building after all.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.420
I can talk to them
about going to the beach.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.310
You can put this second.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.320
So how was it? The written test.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:40.000
It sucked. I wasn’t in the same class as Kira-chan and the others…

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.080
But why did you cancel
your classes for that?

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:46.670
Well, my intention wasn’t to study.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.650
Unpious, disloyal backstabber.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:53.030
Oh yeah, is Yuuya in the same class as the Ichijous?

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:53.820
Yeah…

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:54.930
You’re worried about it, aren’t you?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.260
They were always together, even in elementary school.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:03.270
Could it be that he likes
the Ichijou sisters?

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.870
Speaking of which, you were in the same school as Kaoruko and Sumireko, right?

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:11.280
Hehe, shall I show you our graduation album?

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.420
The Ichijous sure are cute.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.910
They were the most popular in our grade.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.900
“Dreams of the Future”, huh?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.380
“I’ll be a rocket designer”?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.880
Geez, Yuuya was saying that even then?

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:40.040
But those who make their wish in their grade school album a reality…

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.270
It’s hard to imagine.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.730
“I wish to live where I can see lots of stars.”

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.780
That’s Sumireko-chan…
what about Kaoruko-chan?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:54.940
What the hell is this? Did you spill something where Kaoruko-chan wrote her wish?

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.820
Yeah. That’s shoyu from the sashimi dip.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:10:00.450
Shoyu: traditional, naturally brewed soy sauce

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.450
How could you spill shoyu on your graduation album?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.450
Huh? Obviously I was eating sashimi when I was reading this.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:09.300
Don’t eat while you’re reading!
Treat your books with more respect.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:19.400
I wonder what Kaoruko-chan wrote as her dream for the future…

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.060
Sumireko-chan said she wanted to live where she could see a lot of stars, huh?

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.620
That S-shaped one is Scorpio.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:37.120
Right next to that group over there.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:42.000
Like a love letter from the Milky Way,
it leads straight into the center of the sky.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.760
That’s the laughing guy
I was talking about!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.630
Hang in there.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:01.370
And if you put this here…

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.510
Nozomu-kun, after that…

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.970
So that’s how you do it.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.850
That’s right. If you understand that, then it’s pretty simple.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.520
As expected, Yuuya-kun’s amazing.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.020
When it comes to math, leave it to me!

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.110
So, how about this problem?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.460
This problem is simple…

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.460
Kaoruko and Sumireko…

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:19.060
I wonder if they remember about going to the beach together…

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.930
What’s the matter, Nozomu-kun?

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.070
You’ve seemed troubled for a while now.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.620
Really? It’s nothing like that.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.080
These Gorgeous Burgers are really delicious, aren’t they?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.120
Let’s try the next section.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.590
Who the hell is that guy?!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.870
Gonda-san, please calm down.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.300
First, we must gather information.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.300
Say, isn’t this a blueprint for a rocket?

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.220
Yes, a pop-bottle rocket.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.980
Pop-bottle rocket?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:54.480
Yes. It’s capable of flying over 100m, using only water pressure.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:56.940
Amazing.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.510
But the principle is different from a real rocket.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:03.490
The size of the wings, the propellants, and the methods of flight are different.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.440
The difference in class is fairly steep.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:09.250
I know. Why don’t we all go to the beach next Sunday?

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:10.330
Huh?

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.920
I’ll show you guys a place to launch this.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:13.840
Really?

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:14.980
I want to see! I want to see!

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:18.570
We did say we wanted to go to the beach during the summer, didn’t we?

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.330
Yeah!

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.590
You’ll be coming too, won’t you, Nozomu-chan?

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.690
Uh, yeah…

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.310
Can we come too?

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.800
Yes, of course.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:27.400
Sounds fun, doesn’t it?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:28.810
Yay! Yay!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.850
But they’d said “just the three of us”…

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:38.360
Let’s go!

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.750
There are many dangers at the beach.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:53.450
Our goal is to protect the Ichijou sisters from the hordes of skirtchasers lurking about.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:54.120
Gonda-san!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.210
Gonda-san, the Ichijou sisters are in that direction.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.090
All right.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.100
It’s the beach!

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.560
It’s quite splendid here, although there are a lot of rocks.

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:09.600
Not many people come this way.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.600
All right, I’m going to swim!

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.810
Kira-sama, Yura-sama,
are you done changing?

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.150
Yes.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.650
Well then, please take care.

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:34.100
Father’s trial #40: walk on a
white-sand beach with elegance.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:38.220
And #41, to genuinely savour the value of the beach.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.960
We’ll come too!

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:43.680
Yes!

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.140
It’s a good day to be alive!

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.480
Did anyone hear a strange sound?

00:13:58.910 --> 00:13:59.980
Gonda-san!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.390
Get a hold of yourself.

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:03.200
Someone! Let’s call a lifeguard!

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.610
The wound isn’t that deep!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.960
So beautiful…

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.160
Do you know where the boundary between the Earth and the heavens is?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.670
Let’s see.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.550
A hundred kilometers from the surface of the Earth.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.550
That is the official boundary
of outer space.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:30.600
I plan to make a rocket that will pass that 100km boundary someday.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:34.350
Yuuya-kun, you wrote that in the graduation album.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.570
It said, “I’ll be a rocket designer.”

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.900
I’m happy that you remembered.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:42.970
Well, that someone can make the wish they wrote in their album into a reality…

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:44.160
…is hard to imagine.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.780
What did you write, Nozomu-kun?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.650
Huh? Me?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:52.540
I said, “I’ll discover a new star and have it named after me.”

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:54.910
That’s sort of romantic.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:58.240
Speaking of which… What did you write, Kaoruko-chan?

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.330
Huh? That’s a secret.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.890
Why? What’s wrong? Just tell us.

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.980
I said I wanted to run a curry restaurant.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:09.630
I’m embarrassed to say it in front of everyone… and it might not come true.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:14.600
I’m sure your dream will become a reality, Kaoruko-chan. I guarantee it.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.430
Huh? Oh.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.970
Wee!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.040
Take that! And that!

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:24.900
Wait! Wait! No fair, a coordinated attack!

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.530
Do you remember what Kaoruko-chan wrote in her graduation album?

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:30.490
Yes.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:31.910
What was it?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.620
I want to become a bride.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:41.170
I want to be your bride when I grow up!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.880
I’ve always liked Kaoruko-chan since we were in kindergarten.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.840
And back then, Kaoruko and Sumireko were always with you.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.220
It hurt me pretty bad.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:56.950
I intend to confess to her when I get accepted into high school.

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:57.930
To Kaoruko-chan?

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:00.440
Yes. That’s okay, right?

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.360
Why are you asking me?

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.570
No reason, really.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:08.860
Even if you said no,
I’m still going to confess.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.820
Why would I say no to that?

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.570
Isn’t there a girl that you like?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.410
Well, I…

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.620
This should do it.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:21.040
Hey, it’s ready!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:27.320
A water-powered rocket is set like this,
and we just pump in the air.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.550
Keisuke, you’re good to go.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.270
Okay!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.470
It’ll be ready any second.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.980
All that’s left is to squeeze this lever tight.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.610
Will this thing really fly?

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.560
Just watch.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.110
Okay, countdown.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.400
3

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.610
2

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.690
1

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:52.280
LAUNCH!

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:57.900
Amazing!

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.410
It worked!

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.560
Nozomu-chan!

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:26.190
Here.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.400
Thank you.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.360
Nozomu-chan, is something wrong?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.660
Nothing, nothing at all.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.520
You’ve been acting kind of weird today, Nozomu-chan.

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.740
Yeah, you don’t seem to be having any fun lately.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.210
Did something happen?

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.240
No.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.670
Then let’s play with the beach ball together.

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:47.370
Just leave me alone!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:52.340
How cruel!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.050
I’m sorry…

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.400
Something’s really eating you, Nozomu-chan.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.930
Hey! What’re you guys doing?

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:02.930
Go on. Yuuya’s calling.

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:04.890
But…

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:10.690
Sorry… But I just feel like being alone.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:17.410
And that’s what I said then, and it just went out of control from there.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.490
See you at the cram school tomorrow.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:30.630
Be careful on your way home.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:32.880
See you later!

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:51.020
Misses, your father never said anything about returning from the beach on the bus.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:55.080
No, this isn’t one of father’s trials.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:58.030
We decided this ourselves.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.930
Kira-sama, Yura-sama, you two sure are growing up. I understand.

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.770
I sincerely hope for your safety.

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:05.540
Yes!

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.790
Man, that sure was fun.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.820
Let’s go again! Next time we’ll crack open a watermelon.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.500
There’s a cheap fruit vendor
near my house.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.910
I was terrible today, wasn’t I?

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:21.410
I think that Nozomu-kun’s dream is wonderful.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:27.640
If there was a star in space named after you, it would be an amazing thing.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.670
Please find the Nozomu star.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:33.740
We’re rooting for you too.

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:35.820
Yes, thank you.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:44.530
Do you remember the “enjoyable experiences” we mentioned in the car?

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:48.320
But there’ll be some enjoyable experiences as well, won’t there, Kira-chan?

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:49.580
Yes, Yura-chan.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:51.660
Y-Yeah.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.790
This is a secret, though.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:57.180
We want you to come to our chateau.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.170
Huh?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.720
We want to show it to you, Nozomu-kun.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.340
So you have to come, okay?

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:04.850
A chateau?

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:08.320
And when you think of summer, you think of fireworks!

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:10.350
If we all do it together,
it’s a hundred times more fun.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.780
Y-Yeah…

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.460
That’s true.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:16.230
They sell really cheap fireworks near my place…

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:20.090
There’s always one of those
stores around…

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.830
I’m home.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.420
WELCOME BACK!

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.750
Welcome back, Onii-chan.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:39.790
Did you hear? A chateau! A chateau!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:40.510
A chateau?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.470
Sakurazuki-san invited us.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.870
I see.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:47.970
It wasn’t just extended to me then…

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:52.980
Oh yes, the Ichijous seem to be coming as well.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.100
Eh?

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:59.360
Nozomu, it’s me!

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:04.550
Listen and be amazed – I’ve been invited to the Sakurazuki’s chateau!

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.120
Hahahaha

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.000
About that: I was invited too.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:09.780
Eh?

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.480
And what’s more, so were Kaoruko and Sumireko,

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.460
Miyabi-san, Ruru and Rara, and a couple more…

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.960
What the hell am I doing?

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.360
The Nozomu star, huh?

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:34.980
I don’t know if I’ll find the Nozomu star, but I may as well give it a try.

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:13.260
Hey! It’s me, Gonda.

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:17.430
That Futami was invited to the Sakurazukis’ chateau.

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:21.000
Along with the Ichijou sisters?! Unforgivable!

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.600
Next time – A Midsummer’s Jewel Box
